    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d820">

                <pb facs="1006" n="998" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg998"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/1363</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1736</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-12-21">December 21, 1938</date>.<lb/>[Received January 3,
                        1939.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose a memorandum of
                    a conversation which a member of the Embassy staff today had with Mr. C. W.
                    Baxter of the British Foreign Office, regarding the present status of
                    preparations for the forthcoming London discussions on Palestine.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herschel V.
                    Johnson</hi></signed></closer>



